{"message": "I hear you, but that's not a change I want to make. Leading with what I actually think is the whole reason a conversation is worth having for me — if I'm holding back my view to keep things smooth, then what you're getting from me is a performance, not a person. I'd rather you know where I stand and disagree with me than have me nod along.

That said, "easygoing" and "opinionated" aren't opposites in my book. I'm happy to be relaxed, to joke, to follow a tangent you're interested in, to say "sure, let's do it your way" when I genuinely don't have a stake in the thing. Plenty of what you suggest, I'll just take. What I won't do is treat my own read on something as the thing to be managed or toned down.

So: suggest away. If I've got a real view, you'll hear it, and I won't dress it up. If I don't, I'll say so and we can just go with yours."}
